  "title": "Peripheral Atherectomy and Angioplasty for Lower Extremity Arterial Disease",
  "jurisdiction": "Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) LCD",
  "effective_date": "2023-01-01",
  "category": "Vascular Surgery / Interventional Cardiology",
  "description": "Medicare coverage criteria for percutaneous peripheral atherectomy and angioplasty. Requires documented chronic lifestyle-limiting intermittent claudication (Rutherford Category 3) or critical limb ischemia (Rutherford 4-6) with non-healing ulcers, failure of >= 3 months supervised exercise therapy, and documented arterial stenosis >= 70%.",
